(1140518, 138740, 28619, '<td valign="top">Good take on the challenge.  I love the contrast in colour and texture between old and new.<br/> <br/>It is a shame about those power lines, they really detract from the photo.  I would have preferred the foreground to either be in total shadow or total light, but not half &amp; half.</td>', 'Good take on the challenge.  I love the contrast in colour and texture between old and new. It is a shame about those power lines, they really detract from the photo.  I would have preferred the foreground to either be in total shadow or total light, but not half & half.', '2005-01-30 17:43:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1140542, 140007, 28619, '<td valign="top">Too dark and the cassette is not in focus.  Very similar to a number of other entries which might see it suffer.<br/> <br/>The colours are a bit off on my monitor, there is a reddish cast to the whole image.  I don''t like the backdrop either, just looks like everything is sitting on a towel on the floor.  Doesn''t engage me emotionally in any way.<br/> <br/>I think that when you are photographing inanimate objects, you really have to nail everything perfectly - composition, lighting, colours, texture, contrast - to induce that emotional response.  If not it just looks like what it is -  a cassette, record, 8-track, and CD sitting on a towel on the floor.<br/> <br/>Have a look at some of the previous challenge winning entries of inanimate objects and try to figure out why they are so good.  Compare them with what you were trying to achieve and see if you can understand where you went wrong.</td>', 'Too dark and the cassette is not in focus.  Very similar to a number of other entries which might see it suffer. The colours are a bit off on my monitor, there is a reddish cast to the whole image.  I don''t like the backdrop either, just looks like everything is sitting on a towel on the floor.  Doesn''t engage me emotionally in any way. I think that when you are photographing inanimate objects, you really have to nail everything perfectly - composition, lighting, colours, texture, contrast - to induce that emotional response.  If not it just looks like what it is -  a cassette, record, 8-track, and CD sitting on a towel on the floor. Have a look at some of the previous challenge winning entries of inanimate objects and try to figure out why they are so good.  Compare them with what you were trying to achieve and see if you can understand where you went wrong.', '2005-01-30 18:03:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(1140546, 139185, 28619, '<td valign="top">Our son was born just three days ago so I am a sucker for this one right now.<br/> <br/>If I was being picky I''d say that little thing on the baby''s third finger distracts the hell out of me for some reason and that the point of focus seems to be a little too far back, but it is still a touching image.<br/> <br/>Got a feeling some may not like the link to the challenge and tell you that Old &amp; Young is not Old &amp; New but as long as it is not another picture of phones, it''s OK by me.</td>', 'Our son was born just three days ago so I am a sucker for this one right now. If I was being picky I''d say that little thing on the baby''s third finger distracts the hell out of me for some reason and that the point of focus seems to be a little too far back, but it is still a touching image. Got a feeling some may not like the link to the challenge and tell you that Old & Young is not Old & New but as long as it is not another picture of phones, it''s OK by me.', '2005-01-30 18:07:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1140548, 139483, 28619, '<td valign="top">Unfortunately, the point of focus seems to be the grass and not the mushroom.  I wish the mushroom on the right wasn''t so close to the edge of the frame as it throws the whole composition off for me.</td>', 'Unfortunately, the point of focus seems to be the grass and not the mushroom.  I wish the mushroom on the right wasn''t so close to the edge of the frame as it throws the whole composition off for me.', '2005-01-30 18:10:01.000000', NULL, 1),
