(1149556, 139749, 19978, '<td valign="top">David, an outstanding picture and one that I would have loved to see ribbon. Can you post more info about how you achieved such a dramatic effect: tones in the sky, contrast, overall impact?? It''s quite striking and now added to my favs!</td>', 'David, an outstanding picture and one that I would have loved to see ribbon. Can you post more info about how you achieved such a dramatic effect: tones in the sky, contrast, overall impact?? It''s quite striking and now added to my favs!', '2005-02-03 19:57:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(1150053, 138640, 9581, '<td valign="top">Hi and welcome to DPC! I noticed your shot when I was reviewing my photos under the <a href="//dpchallenge.com/camera.php?CAMERA_ID=1072" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Fugi  A 3100</a> <br/>This is a nice shot. Your eye for detail has potential to here...<br/>We are all creative in our own ways but it is the camera and functions that help create the best photo it can be... believe me I have had my challenge in learning it too. I still dont always get the image to be quite as good as it should be but thats where the fun comes in.. <br/> <br/>So basically I just wanted to say welcome here as well as say....Anytime you want to trade notes on the usage of this camera or if you have questions that no one on the forums here knows about on using this camera then know that I am around... I have had this particular camera probably since October of 2004. I also have been playing with the white balance, the ISO speed and aperture f2.8- f8 ...The ring is neat with a filters specially the polorizer it enhances photos.  I probably have used only half of the features so far as far as setting them correctly and having a end picture be ok. <br/>:) Anyways its good to see someone else here using the same make of my   camera   here. <br/>And again Welcome aboard to DPC. <br/></td>', 'Hi and welcome to DPC! I noticed your shot when I was reviewing my photos under the Fugi  A 3100 This is a nice shot. Your eye for detail has potential to here...We are all creative in our own ways but it is the camera and functions that help create the best photo it can be... believe me I have had my challenge in learning it too. I still dont always get the image to be quite as good as it should be but thats where the fun comes in..  So basically I just wanted to say welcome here as well as say....Anytime you want to trade notes on the usage of this camera or if you have questions that no one on the forums here knows about on using this camera then know that I am around... I have had this particular camera probably since October of 2004. I also have been playing with the white balance, the ISO speed and aperture f2.8- f8 ...The ring is neat with a filters specially the polorizer it enhances photos.  I probably have used only half of the features so far as far as setting them correctly and having a end picture be ok. :) Anyways its good to see someone else here using the same make of my   camera   here. And again Welcome aboard to DPC. ', '2005-02-04 02:31:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(1151039, 138706, 8860, '<td valign="top">I''ve been looking to achieve this shot for some time now  (only ever saw these two face-on) and never really explored it - so I never knew you could get this view! It''s superb.</td>', 'I''ve been looking to achieve this shot for some time now  (only ever saw these two face-on) and never really explored it - so I never knew you could get this view! It''s superb.', '2005-02-04 18:18:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(1151548, 138515, 31214, '<td valign="top">I think you said it yourself....if you can''t see the old posts with this size, then how are we to see it?  I like the picture, but when i voted, I saw no relevance to the theme.</td>', 'I think you said it yourself....if you can''t see the old posts with this size, then how are we to see it?  I like the picture, but when i voted, I saw no relevance to the theme.', '2005-02-05 03:41:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(1151734, 138442, 23478, '<td valign="top">To me, this was a fun shot.  I did a bit of a rush job as has been pointed out to me.  There is the upper right corner of the photo and the drop cloth is all wrinkled, the lighting is too strong... that''s what happens when you wait to until the last minute to do the shot.  Also, I was using my four month old as a model and trying to keep my 3 year old &amp; 5 year old from getting too close.  So, all in all, it turned out OK, but I know I could have done better.  <br/> <br/>Thanks for all the thoughts and comments.</td>', 'To me, this was a fun shot.  I did a bit of a rush job as has been pointed out to me.  There is the upper right corner of the photo and the drop cloth is all wrinkled, the lighting is too strong... that''s what happens when you wait to until the last minute to do the shot.  Also, I was using my four month old as a model and trying to keep my 3 year old & 5 year old from getting too close.  So, all in all, it turned out OK, but I know I could have done better.   Thanks for all the thoughts and comments.', '2005-02-05 07:09:21.000000', NULL, 0),
